# Citation File Format (https://citation-file-format.github.io), seeded by
# swarm-routing/.github org-sync (`citation = true`; `citation_type` and
# `[[references]]` in .github/org-sync.toml); the repository's own once
# written. Commitizen keeps `version:` in step (`.cz.toml` version_files
# "CITATION.cff:^version:"); swarm-routing/.github tools/zenodo reads the
# concept DOI from `doi:` once the first release is archived on Zenodo.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Termite"
abstract: >-
  Termite (Roth & Wicker, 2003/2005) as a standalone swarm routing protocol
  for MANETs: routing by stigmergy, pheromone carried inside data packets, no
  control ants, randomised multipath forwarding. A simulator-agnostic C++ core
  and an ns-3 contrib module on swarm-core.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Joppi
    given-names: Daniel Henrique
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-6436-8174"
version: "0.1.0"
# The work as a whole; core/ also MIT OR GPL-2.0-only (LICENSING.md).
license: GPL-2.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/swarm-routing/Termite"
url: "https://github.com/swarm-routing/Termite"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24124722"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.24124722"
    description: "Concept DOI: always resolves to the latest released version."
references:
  - type: thesis
    title: "Termite: A Swarm Intelligent Routing Algorithm For Mobile Wireless Ad-Hoc Networks"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Roth"
        given-names: "Martin"
    institution:
      name: "Cornell University"
    thesis-type: "PhD thesis"
    year: 2005
    url: "https://hdl.handle.net/1813/240"
    notes: "Roth's dissertation, as deposited in Cornell eCommons: the primary source this repository implements (ch. 4); docs/fidelity.md maps it to the code. Degree and school from the dissertation's title page; the eCommons record names neither. No DOI: none registered."
  - type: software
    title: "ns3-swarm-core"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Joppi"
        given-names: "Daniel Henrique"
    year: 2026
    publisher:
      name: "Zenodo"
    doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24138628"
    notes: "The shared primitives core/ builds on (pinned by release: swarm-core.lock) and the ns-3 base the adapter derives from (SwarmRoutingBase)."
